  "feature_instruction": "This feature, 'Frontend: Membership & Account', provides the user interface for viewing available membership plans and managing an authenticated user's personal account, including their current membership and booked classes. It integrates with the `membership-payment-be` and `class-scheduling-be` backend features to fetch and update data.\n\n## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A1A1A] text-[#F5F5F5]\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#DFFF00] hover:bg-[#c2e600] text-[#1A1A1A] font-bold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Secondary CTA: bg-[#333333] hover:bg-[#1A1A1A] text-[#F5F5F5] font-semibold rounded-full px-6 py-2 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#DFFF00]\n- Section bg: bg-[#F5F5F5] (light sections) / bg-[#1A1A1A] (dark sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-[#F5F5F5]\n- Body: text-gray-700 leading-relaxed\n- Hero Image: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534438327276-14e5300c3a48?w=1920&q=80\n\n### 1. `frontend/src/types/membership.ts`\nThis file defines the TypeScript interfaces and types for membership plans, user memberships, and related entities. These types are derived directly from the backend DTOs exposed by the `membership-payment-be` and `class-scheduling-be` features. It includes `MembershipPlanDto`, `User` (a minimal representation for DTOs), `MembershipStatus` (string literal union), `UserMembershipDto`, `GymClassDto`, and `BookingStatus` (string literal union), and `ClassBookingDto`.\n\n### 2. `frontend/src/services/membershipService.ts`\nThis service acts as the data access layer for membership-related operations, making API calls to the `membership-payment-be` backend. It uses the `axios` instance from `frontend/src/api/client.ts` for authenticated requests.\n- **`getAllMembershipPlans()`**: Fetches all active membership plans. It calls `GET /api/v1/memberships/plans` and expects a `List<MembershipPlanDto>` as a response.\n- **`getUserMembership()`**: Fetches the authenticated user's current active membership. It calls `GET /api/v1/memberships/my-membership` and expects a `UserMembershipDto` as a response, or `null` if no active membership is found.\n- **`purchaseMembership(planId: string)`**: Initiates the purchase of a membership plan for the authenticated user. It calls `POST /api/v1/memberships/purchase/{planId}` (where `{planId}` is the UUID of the plan) and expects a `UserMembershipDto` as a response.\n\n### 3. `frontend/src/hooks/useMemberships.ts`\nThis file provides React Query hooks for managing membership data, abstracting the `membershipService.ts` calls and providing caching, loading, and error states to components.\n- **`useAllMembershipPlans()`**: A `useQuery` hook that fetches all active membership plans using `membershipService.getAllMembershipPlans()`. It returns `QueryObserverResult<MembershipPlanDto[], Error>`.\n- **`useUserMembership()`**: A `useQuery` hook that fetches the authenticated user's current membership using `membershipService.getUserMembership()`. It returns `QueryObserverResult<UserMembershipDto | null, Error>`.\n- **`usePurchaseMembership()`**: A `useMutation` hook that allows purchasing a membership plan using `membershipService.purchaseMembership(planId)`. It returns `UseMutationResult<UserMembershipDto, Error, string>`.\n\n### 4. `frontend/src/pages/MembershipsPage.tsx`\nThis page displays all available membership plans to users. It uses the `Layout` component from `shared-ui` and leverages the `useAllMembershipPlans` hook to fetch data. The page content is structured as follows:\n- Wraps content in `<Layout>`. The main content area uses `<section className=\"py-16 px-4 bg-[#1A1A1A] text-[#F5F5F5]\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">`.\n- **Hero Section**: A full-width hero image (using the provided Unsplash URL: `https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534438327276-14e5300c3a48?w=1920&q=80`) with a dark overlay (`<div className=\"absolute inset-0 bg-black bg-opacity-50\" />`). Contains a bold headline: `<h1 className=\"text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-[#F5F5F5] mb-4\">Unlock Your Potential with MultiFit Aundh Memberships</h1>` and a motivational subheadline: `<p className=\"text-xl text-[#F5F5F5] mb-8\">Choose the plan that powers your fitness journey.</p>`.\n- **Membership Plans Section**: Displays membership plans in a grid or pricing table format. Each plan is presented in a card (`bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6`).\n  - Each card displays `name`, `description`, `price` (formatted as currency), and `durationInMonths` from `MembershipPlanDto`.\n  - Each card includes a "Join Now" button (`<button className=\"bg-[#DFFF00] hover:bg-[#c2e600] text-[#1A1A1A] font-bold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\">Join Now</button>`) that, when clicked, triggers the `usePurchaseMembership` mutation with the corresponding `planId`. Upon successful purchase, the user should be redirected to the `/account` page.\n- Loading and error states should be handled gracefully, displaying a loading spinner or an error message.\n\n### 5. `frontend/src/pages/AccountPage.tsx`\nThis page serves as the authenticated user's personal dashboard, displaying their current membership status and booked classes. It uses the `Layout` component from `shared-ui` and leverages the `useUserMembership` hook from this feature and the `useBookings` hook from the `class-booking-ui` feature.\n- Wraps content in `<Layout>`. The main content area uses `<section className=\"py-16 px-4 bg-[#F5F5F5] text-gray-700\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">`.\n- **Account Overview Section**: Contains a heading: `<h1 className=\"text-3xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A] mb-8\">My MultiFit Account</h1>`.\n- **Current Membership Section**: Displays the user's active membership details.\n  - Uses `useUserMembership` to fetch `UserMembershipDto`.\n  - If an active membership exists, display: `membershipPlan.name`, `membershipPlan.description`, `startDate`, `endDate`, and `status`.\n  - If no active membership, display a message like \"You don't have an active membership.\" and a CTA to \"Explore Memberships\" (`<a href=\"/memberships\" className=\"bg-[#DFFF00] hover:bg-[#c2e600] text-[#1A1A1A] font-bold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\">Explore Memberships</a>`).\n- **Booked Classes Section**: Displays a list of classes the user has booked.\n  - Uses the `useBookings().useUserBookings()` hook (from `class-booking-ui`) to fetch `ClassBookingDto[]`.\n  - For each `ClassBookingDto`, display `gymClass.name`, `gymClass.date`, `gymClass.startTime`, `gymClass.trainerName`, and `bookingTime`.\n  - Provide an option to cancel a booking (this would involve calling a mutation from `useBookings` in `class-booking-ui`).\n- Loading and error states should be handled gracefully.",
